    "answer": {
      "short": "$0.05<\\frac{3}{8}<45\\%<0.9<130\\%<\\frac{7}{4}$. Use a scale from $0$ to $2$; positions are shown on the number line.",
      "worked": "Convert to decimal form:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{3}{8}&=0.375\\\\45\\%&=0.45\\\\\\frac{7}{4}&=1.75\\\\130\\%&=1.3\\end{align*}$$\nThe other two numbers are already decimals. Order by place value:\n$$0.05<0.375<0.45<0.9<1.3<1.75.$$\nRewrite in the original forms:\n$$0.05<\\frac{3}{8}<45\\%<0.9<130\\%<\\frac{7}{4}.$$\nUse a scale from $0$ to $2$ and place each value at its corresponding decimal position, as shown.",
      "solutionDiagrams": [
        {
          "id": "v2-5458e-p51-practice-slot-29-slot-29-solution-number-line",
          "role": "solution",
          "format": "tikz",
